Affected component: OSPF virtual-link between r4 and r8. After r4 reloaded, its OSPF lost the virtual-link configuration that connects r8 (ABR for Areas 1 and 2) to the backbone (Area 0) through Area 1.

Mechanism: r8 originates Area 2 routes (18.x.x.x loopbacks and 80.0.0.0/8) and must inject them into Area 0 via a virtual-link to r4 across Area 1. With the virtual-link down on r4, r8’s Area 2 summary-LSAs are not flooded into the backbone, so r1 never installs those prefixes. Area 1 remains healthy, so r1 still learns Area 1 routes (e.g., 58.0.0.0/8) and all Area 0 routes.

